# ⛔ Agent worktrees live here, and each one is itself a git repository. A
# `git add -A` records such a directory as a GITLINK — a commit id and nothing
# else — silently, for every one it finds. One nearly went up with this commit.
#
# The barrier is the pre-push guard, which refuses an undeclared gitlink; this
# entry is the convenience that keeps them out of `git status` in the first
# place.
/.claude/
